        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Second Battle of Panipat</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">5 November 1556</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">Panipat, north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, not far from the site of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-battle-of-panipat">First Battle of Panipat</a> of 1526</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a> under the 13-year-old <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akbar">Akbar</a> and his guardian Bairam Khan, with the field army led by Ali Quli Khan Shaibani; Hemchandra (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hemu">Hemu</a>) and his Afghan army, numerically superior, with a 30,000-strong cavalry force and an elephant contingent numbering 500, and no artillery</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hemu">Hemu</a> was wounded by an arrow and fell unconscious, and his army broke and fled. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a> won, and Hemu was captured and beheaded.</span></div>
